Z||000020||Formula||03-01-2000||09:21 PM||||88 Formula V6 auto <BR>20 mpg Without EGR BackRoad 94 oct fuel<BR>23 mpg With EGR BackRoad 94 oct fuel<BR>20 mpg Without EGR HighWay at 71 mph 94 oct.<BR>25 mpg With EGR Highway at 71 mph 87 oct.<BR>10-15 mpg Driven Hard 94 oct fuel<BR>18 mpg Extreme Twisties 94 oct fuel<P>I have had my EGR tube hooked up with 5/8" heaterhose for 400 miles now and it seems to be holding up.  I also replaced the small vacuum hose on the top part with winshield washer hose.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000021||fiero56||03-01-2000||10:15 PM||||I just filled up this evening. <BR>1988 Formula(v-6, 5-speed). Average speed around 70mph. I got 27mpg on the last tank. I have seen it much better(in the low 30s) but there is a very long hill on I-75(Daytonians know what I'm talking about) that I drive up twice a day. Not to mention the stop and go traffic I'm stuck in on the highway everyday once I get downtown. So, real "highway drving" is usually around 33-34mpg.||||reg||1
Z||000022||Standard||03-03-2000||06:26 PM||||After driving 70 miles at about 70mph, I got 26 miles per gallon.  86 GT 5spd.  143,000 miles on the engine...<P>Around town I don't see over 15 mpg, tho?  I just replace the 02 sensor before the trip.. i know I need to give the thing a major tune up...||||reg||1
Z||000023||88formula||03-03-2000||10:57 PM||||I’ve checked mine twice on my 88 formula five speed. The first time was 29mpg mostly highway with some heavy throttle stop and go in between and the second time was mostly city which was 23mpg. The best I ever got with my slow 87 four cylinder puke was 21 mostly highway driven conservatively.||||reg||1
Z||000024||88formula||03-03-2000||11:00 PM||||I’ve checked mine twice on my 88 formula five speed. The first time was 29mpg mostly highway with some heavy throttle stop and go in between and the second time was mostly city which was 23mpg. The best I ever got with my slow 87 four cylinder auto puke was 21mpg mostly highway driven conservatively. I could never figure out why that was so.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Phaeton||03-04-2000||03:06 AM||||My 88GT normally gets 22 mpg.  But driving from Haines to Fairbanks the last five hundred miles are all downhill,  thirteen gallons! For awhile I thought it must be the Canadian gasoline.  CC set on eightyfive mph too.||||reg||12
Z||000026||Dan||03-05-2000||06:50 PM|||| I have an 86 SE auto. Just checked yesterday<BR>and its about 26 mpg at 70mph.Haven't checked in town yet.Definately replace the o2 sensor. It detects the amount of o2 in the exhaust and the feedbact to the computer<BR>also considering engine temp,rpm,throttle position,vacuum,and atmospheric pressure will determine what fuel ratio the injectors will deliver.This is the open loop mode the computer will deliver.I think the open loop mode considers all the inputs and the closed loop refers to the operating data supplied by the eeprom thus the default settings.At various moments the computer will supply from 12.5-15:1 air/fuel ratio,when in the open loop mode.The closed loop mode more or less supplies a fuel-air mixture somewhere in between,but not the optimun mixture for performance and mileage that we have all come to love.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Patrick's Dad||03-05-2000||08:15 PM||||88 Formula 5Sp.<P>I remember at one point averaging 28mpg... that was before reformulated gas, an underdrive pulley, 225's on the rear, a larger catcon, and straight pipes. Now, I get just over 22.<P>I had an '85 2m4 that got 32 combined... before the clutch, rear calipers, and ECM all went at once.||||reg||2
